$DATUM A suspension of
6-bromo-5-fluoro-4-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-ylamino)quinoline-3-carbonitrile
(280 mg, 0.8 mmol), 3-pyridinylboronic acid (118 mg, 1.0 mmol) and sodium
carbonate (130 mg, 1.2 mmol) in dioxane:water (9:1, 5 mL) was purged with
nitrogen for 10 min. Tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (92 mg, 0.08
mmol) was added and the mixture was heated to 90 °C for 3 h. The reaction
was then concentrated to give a residue which was purified by FC.
5-fluoro-6-(pyridin-3-yl)-4-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-ylamino)quinoline-3-
carbonitrile as an off white solid (185 mg, 66%). m/z 349 (M+H)+.
