$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
7-(2,3-O-Isopropylidene-5-O-tert-butyldimethylsilyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-4-phenyl-7H-pyrrolo[
2,3-d]pyrimidine (10d). An argon purged mixture of compound 8 (309 mg,
0.7 mmol), phenylboronic acid (128 mg, 1.05 mmol), K2CO3 (193 mg, 1.4
mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (41 mg, 0.035 mmol) in toluene (5 mL) was stirred at
100 °C for 5 h. The mixture was diluted with chloroform (20 mL) and
washed with aqueous NH4Cl (sat., 20 mL). The aqueous phase was
re-extracted with chloroform (2×5 mL) and the combined organic extracts
dried over MgSO4, concentrated in vacuo and the residue chromatographed
on silica (hexanes-AcOEt, 10:1→7:1) to afford 10d (320 mg, 95%) as a
colorless oil.
5-Fluoro-4-(furan-3-yl)-7-(2,3,5-tri-O-benzoyl-β-D-ribofuranosyl)-7H-pyrrolo[2,3-
d]pyrimidine (13m). Compound 13m was prepared as described for 10d by
coupling compound 12 and furane-3-boronic acid. A colorless foam was
obtained after chromatography on silica (hexanes-AcOEt, 10:1→7:1). Yield
66%. 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): 4.68 (dd, 1H, J gem= 12.2, J 5´b,4´= 3.7,
H-5´b); 4.80 (ddd, 1H,J 4´,3´ = 4.1, J 4´,5´ = 3.7, 3.0 H-4´); 4.88 (dd,
1H, J gem= 12.1,J 5´a,4´ = 3.0, H-5´a); 6.09 (dd, 1H, J 3´,2´ = 5.8, J
3´,4´ = 4.1, H-3´); 6.14 (dd, 1H, J 2´,1´ = 6.1, J 2´,3´ = 5.8, H-2´);
6.84 (dd, 1H, J 1´,2´ = 6.1, J H,F = 1.3, H-1´); 7.17 (d, 1H, J H,F =
2.2, H-6); 7.18 (dd, 1H, J 4,5 = 1.8, J H,F = 0.7, H-4-furyl); 7.36, 7.42
and 7.51 (3 × m, 3 × 2H, H-m-Bz); 7.54 (dd, 1H,J 5,4 = 1.8, J 5,2 = 1.6,
H-5-furyl); 7.54, 7.60 and 7.63 (3 × m, 3 × 1H, H-p-Bz); 7.93, 8.02 and
8.15 (3 × m, 3 × 2H, H-o-Bz); 8.32 (dd, 1H, J 2,5= 1.6, J H,F = 0.7,
H-2-furyl); 8.83 (s, 1H, H-2). 13C NMR (151 MHz, CDCl3): 63.76 (CH2-5´);
71.42 (CH-3´); 73.64 (CH-2´); 80.25 (CH-4´); 85.34 (CH-1´); 105.29 (d, J
C,F = 15, C-4a); 108.01 (d, J C,F = 31, CH-6); 109.75 (d, J C,F = 6,
CH-4-furyl); 124.39 (C-3-furyl); 128.30 (C-i- Bz); 128.47 and 128.54
(CH-m-Bz); 128.60 (C-i-Bz); 128.72 (CH-m-Bz); 129.23 (C-i-Bz); 129.66,
129.81 and 129.82 (CH-o-Bz); 133.57 and 133.76 (CH-p-Bz); 142.88 (d, J
C,F = 251, C-5); 143.76 (CH-5-furyl); 145.53 (d, J C,F = 15, CH-2-furyl);
147.95 (d, J C,F = 3, C-7a); 150.99 (d, J C,F = 4, C-4); 152.38 (CH-2);
165.11, 165.42 and 166.14 (CO). 19F NMR (470.3 MHz, CDCl3): -160.62. MS
FAB, m/z (rel. %): 648 (100)[M+H]. HR MS (FAB): calcd for C36H27FN3O8
[M+H] 648.1782, found 648.1807.
