$DATUM 5-(1,3-Dimethy1H-pyrazo4-yl)-3-{(1R)-1-[5-fluoro-2-(2H-1,2,3-triazo2-yl)phenyl]ethoxy}pyridin-2-amine
(7a). A mixture of 16 (75 mg, 0.2 mmol),
1,3-dimethy4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy[1,3,2]-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole
(74.8 mg, 0.34 mmol), and cesium fluoride (91.1 mg, 0.91 mmol) was taken
up in methanol (2 mL), and the solution was thoroughly degassed.
PdCl2(dppf) (8.2 mg, 0.01 mmol) was added to the solution, and the
reaction was heated in the microwave at 120 °C for 1 h. The reaction was
allowed to cool, and the filtrate was passed through a 2 μm syringe
filter prior to being purified by SFC to afford 7a. Colorless solid,
yield 51 mg, 66%. LC-MS (APCI) m/z 394 (M + H)+; 1H NMR (600 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 8.23 (s, 2H), 7.66 (dd, J = 8.88, 5.10 Hz, 1H), 7.58 (dd, J =
9.82, 3.02 Hz, 1H), 7.54 (s, 1H), 7.48 (d, J = 1.51 Hz, 1H), 7.33 (td, J
= 8.50, 3.02 Hz, 1H), 6.56 (d, J = 1.89 Hz, 1H), 5.86 (s, 2H), 5.53 (q, J
= 6.29 Hz, 1H), 3.72 (s, 3H), 1.94 (s, 3H), 1.58 (d, J = 6.42 Hz, 3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Design of Potent and Selective Inhibitors to Overcome Clinical Anaplastic
Lymphoma Kinase Mutations Resistant to Crizotinib
