$DATUM Nitrogen was bubbled through a suspension of 69 (489 mg, 0.56 mmol; see
the Supporting Information), tert-butyl
[(3-bromo-6-methylimidazo[1,2-a]pyrimidin-2-yl)methyl]methylcarbamate
(75) (197 mg, 0.57 mmol; see the Supporting Information), and CsF (253
mg, 1.66 mmol) in toluene (3.7 mL) for a period of 10 min. To the mixture
was added PdCl2·dppf (45.7 mg, 0.06 mmol), and the reaction was heated at
reflux for 14 h. The reaction was allowed to cool and diluted with EtOAc
(20 mL). The organic phase was washed with water (2 × 5 mL) and brine (5
mL) and dried over MgSO4. The solution was filtered and concentrated and
the residue purified by column chromatography on silica gel eluting with
0-100% EtOAc/ heptanes. Methyl
2-[(1R)-1-({3-[bis(tert-butoxycarbonyl)-amino]-6-(2-{[(tert-butoxycarbonyl)methylamino]methyl}-6-cyanoimidazo[1,2-a]pyridin-3-yl)pyrazin-2-yl}oxy)ethyl]-4-fluoroben-zoate.
Yield: (288 mg, 66%), viscous oil. LC-MS (APCI) m/z 765.3 [M + H]+; 1H
NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 8.46 (s, 1 H), 8.20 (s, 2 H), 7.97 (dd, J = 8.7,
6.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.44-7.33 (m, 2 H), 7.28-7.21 (m, 1 H), 6.41-6.30 (m, 1 H),
4.45-4.25 (m, 2 H), 3.82 (s, 3 H), 2.74 (s, 3 H), 2.28 (s, 3 H), 1.61 (d,
J = 6.3 Hz, 3 H), 1.47 (s, 18 H), 1.30 (br s, 9 H).
