$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Methyl (R)-1-Formyl-6-(2-furyl)-1,2,3,4-tetrahydropyridine-2-carboxylate
(6e) Methyl (R)-6-bromo-1-formyl-1,2,3,4-tetrahydropyridine-2-carboxylate
3 (100 mg, 0.40 mmol) was dissolved in DMF (5 mL) and the 2-furylboronic
acid (67 mg, 0.60 mmol) and Et3N (0.17 mL, 1.61 mmol) were added. The
flask was flushed with argon and the contents were subjected to freeze,
pump, and thaw cycles in order to degas it completely. PdCl2(PPh3)2 (14.2
mg, 0.02 mmol) was added and the resulting mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 16 hours. The completion of reaction was monitored by
TLC. The reaction was quenched by addition of water and extracted with
dichloromethane. The combined organic phases were dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate. After the drying agent was filtered off, the filtrate was
evaporated to dryness in vacuo, and the residue was purified by column
chromatography (EtOAc: n-pentane; 1:1) on silica gel. Yellow oil; (62 mg,
66%). [α]D = +9.5 (c = 1, CHCl3). Rf 0.43 (EtOAc: n-pentane; 1:1). 1H NMR
(500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 8.39 (s, 1H, CHO), 7.36 (m, 1H, CH), 6.37 (m, 1H,
CH), 6.36 (m, 1H, CH), 5.39-5.36 (m, 2H, CH), 3.67 (s, 3H, COOCH3), 2.37
(m, 1H, CH2), 2.23-2.13 (m, 2H, CH2), 1.87 (m, 1H, CH2). 13C NMR (125.7
MHz, CDCl3) δ 170.5 (COO), 161.0 (CHO), 148.5(C), 142.8 (C), 128.3 (CH),
112.3 (CH), 111.0 (CH) 109.5 (CH), 52.6 (CHCOO), 50.2 (COOCH3), 23.5
(CH2), 20.2 (CH2). C12H13NO4 (235.08). HRMS (EI): m/z = 235.08277;
calcd.: m/z = 235.08391.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
