$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-(8-bromo-2,3-diphenylquinoxalin-5-yl)thiophene-2-carbaldehyde (2)
Compound 1 (1.06 g, 2.4 mmol), 10 mL of 2.0 M K2CO3 aqueous solution and
a catalytic amount Pd(PPh3)4 (5 mole %) in 20 mL THF were heated to
reflux for 0.5 h and then injected 10 mL THF containing
(5-formylthiophen-2-yl)boronic acid (300 mg, 1.9 mmol). After refluxed
for 12 h, the mixture was poured into water and extracted with CH2Cl2
(3x10 mL). The organic portion was combined and removed by rotary
evaporation. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
using dichloromethane as eluent.
5-(8-(4-(2',4'-bis(hexyloxy)-[1,1'-biphenyl]-4-yl)-1,2,3,3a,4,8b-hexahydrocyclopenta[b]indo7-yl)-2,3-diphenylquinoxalin-5-yl)thiophene-2-carbaldehyde
(3) The synthetic procedure for compound 3 was followed using 2 (71 mg,
0.15 mmol), 2.0 M K2CO3 aqueous solution (8 mL) and a catalytic amount
Pd(PPh3)4 (5 mole %) in 16 mL of THF were heated to reflux for 0.5 h and
then injected 8 mL THF containing
4-(2',4'-bis(hexyloxy)-[1,1'-biphenyl]-4-yl)-7-(4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1,2,3,3a,4,8b-hexahydrocyclopenta[b]indole
(96 mg, 0.15 mmol). The pure product was separated by a silica gel column
chromatography using pure dichloromethane to yield 90 mg of a red solid
(yield 66.5 %). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz), δ (TMS, ppm): 0.89-0.99 (m, 6H),
1.33-1.43 (m, 8H), 1.45-1.55 (m, 4H), 1.70-1.87 (m, 6H), 1.90-2.00 (m,
1H), 2.05-2.14 (m, 2H), 2.15-2.22 (m, 1H), 3.94-4.06 (m, 5H), 4.90-4.96
(m, 1H), 6.57-6.62 (m, 2H), 7.20-7.24 (m, 1H), 7.28-7.40 (m, 6H),
7.43-7.47 (m, 3H), 7.56-7.62 (m, 3H), 7.66-7.70 (m, 2H), 7.77-7.81 (m,
3H), 7.82 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.87 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 7.92 (d, J = 4.1
Hz, 1H), 8.21 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 9.99 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 100
MHz), δ (TMS, ppm): 14.1, 14.1, 22.6, 24.6, 25.8, 29.1, 31.5, 45.5, 68.1,
68.4, 69.1, 100.4, 105.3, 107.8, 118.8, 123.1, 126.6, 127.8, 127.8,
128.2, 128.3, 128.4, 128.7, 129.0, 129.2, 130.2, 130.4, 130.8, 131.8,
134.9, 135.8, 137.5, 138.5, 138.6, 138.9, 141.0, 141.2, 144.6, 147.7,
149.0, 151.6, 151.7, 157.0, 159.5, 183.4. HRMS (APCI, m/z): [M+H]+ calcd.
for (C60H60N3O3S): 902.4355; found: 902.4315.
