$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure C. A microwave vial was
charged with bromide (0.25 mmol), benzimidazole (0.26 mmol), Pd(OAc)2
(2.80 mg, 12.5 μmol), XPhos (12 mg, 25 μmol), and Et3N (70 μL, 0.50
mmol). The reaction vessel was sealed, then evacuated and backfilled with
argon 3 times. After dissolving the reaction mixture in 1.4 mL of
degassed EtOH, the reaction mixture was allowed to stir at 85 °C for 16
h. The mixture was filtered through Celite and the filter cake was washed
with EtOAc (6 mL). The filtrate was concentrated and purified on a silica
gel column to yield pure product.
5-Methyl-2-(5-(pyridin-3-yl)furan-2-yl)-1H-benzo[d]imidazole. Following
general procedure C, 3-bromopyridine (40 mg, 25 μL) and 2e (79 mg) were
allowed to react to give 45.2 mg of the title compound (66% yield) as a
light-yellow solid. mp >260 °C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.82 (s, 1 H),
8.38 (d, J = 5.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.63 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 7.20 (d, J = 4.0
Hz, 1 H), 7.10-7.60 (m, 2 H), 7.08 (dd, J = 8.0, 4.5 Hz, 1 H), 7.01 (d, J
= 8.0 Hz, 1 H), 6.75 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1 H), 2.39 (s, 3 H); 13C NMR (125
MHz, CDCl3) δ 151.5, 148.0, 146.3, 144.8, 143.6, 133.1, 131.4, 126.3,
124.7, 123.8, 112.4, 109.4, 21.8; FTIR (neat) ν 2921, 1636, 1430, 1222,
960, 852; HRMS (ESI) m/z calcd for C17H14N3O (MH)+ 276.1137, found
276.1126.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used, Suzuki coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Oxidative Condensations To Form Benzimidazole-Substituted Potassium
Organotrifluoroborates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Molander, Gary A.; Ajayi, Kehinde
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(16), 4242-4245

