$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-Chloro-4-(2-chloropyridin-3-yl)-5-fluoropyrimidine (S1). To
2,4-dichloro-5-fluoropyrimidine (2.960 g, 18 mmol),
2-chloropyridin-3-ylboronic acid (4.2 g, 27 mmol), and
tetrakis(triphenylphosphine) palladium (2.0 g, 1.8 mmol) was added 36 mL
of DME followed by aqueous sodium bicarbonate (1.0 M, 18 mL, 18 mmol).
The resulting mixture was heated to 90 °C in a sealed tube for 18 h. Upon
cooling to RT the mixture was diluted with EtOAc and saturated sodium
bicarbonate. The organic portion was washed with water, dried over sodium
sulfate, filtered and concentrated. The crude material was purified by
silica gel chromatography (10-50% EtOAc/hex). The product containing
fractions were combined and concentrated to yield
2-chloro-4-(2-chloropyridin-3-yl)-5-fluoropyrimidine (2.96 g, 12 mmol,
66% yield) as a light yellow solid.
2-Chloro-4-(2-chloropyridin-3-yl)-5-fluoropyrimidine (S1), yield 2.96 g,
12 mmol, 66% MS: m/z 245.1 ([M+H]+). 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ
9.14-9.13 (m, 1H), 8.67-8.66 (m, 1H), 8.17-8.15 (m, 1H), 7.71-7.68 (m,
1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Suzuki coupling, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Potent, Selective, and Orally Bioavailable
Pyridinyl-Pyrimidine Phthalazine Aurora Kinase Inhibitor
