$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Bromo-3-(1H-indol-5-yl)-1-tosyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (17). To a
stirred suspension of 16 (60 g, 125 mmol) and 1H-indol-5-ylboronic acid
(22.2 g, 138 mmol) in CH3CN (625 mL) was added 1 M Na2 CO3 (312 mL)
followed by bis(triphenylphosphine)-palladium(II) dichloride (4.4 g, 6.2
mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred at room temperature for 1 h.
After complete consumption of starting materials, the mixture was
extracted with EtOAc and evaporated to dryness in vacuo, it was dissolved
in CH2Cl2 (50 mL), absorbed onto Celite, and dried. The residue was
purified via silica gel chromatography using CH2Cl2 as the eluent. 17
(38.6 g, 65% yield). 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6, 300 MHz): δ 11.21 (bs, 1H), 8.52
(d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.47 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 8.13 (s, 1H), 8.05 (d, J =
5.1 Hz, 2H), 7.92 (s, 1H), 7.51 (d, J = 4.8 Hz, 1H), 7.46 (dd, J = 5.1,
1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.43 (d, J = 5.1 Hz, 1H), 7.40 (dd, J = 3.9, 1.8 Hz, 2H),
6.52 (dd, J = 2.7, 1.2 Hz,1 H), 2.33 (s, 3H). MS ESI (m/z): 466.2/468.2
(M + H)+, calcd 466.
