$DATUM (S)-2′-Amino-3-(6,6-dimethyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-5′Hspiro[
chromeno[2,3-b]pyridine-5,4′-oxazol]-7-ol (18b). A microwave reaction
vial was charged with
(S)-2′-amino-3-bromo-5′H-spiro-[chromeno[2,3-b]pyridine-5,4′-oxazol]-7-ol
(0.850 g, 2.441 mmol),
2-(2,2-dimethyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(as a 1.5:1 mixture of olefin isomers, 0.930 g, 3.91 mmol), potassium
carbonate (1.012 g, 7.32 mmol) and PdCl2(AmPhos)2 (0.086 g, 0.122 mmol),
1,4-dioxane (14.24 mL), and water (2.035 mL). The vial was sealed and
heated in microwave reactor for 1 h at 100°C. The reaction mixture was
diluted with water and washed with EtOAc. The aqueous layer was extracted
with EtOAc, and the combined organic layers were dried with sodium
sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. The residue was purified via column
chromatography on silica gel (0-80% of a 90:10:1 mixture of DCM/
MeOH/NH4OH in DCM). The resulting material was repurified to collect the
title regiosomer as the first eluting peak.
(S)-2′-amino-3-(6,6-dimethyl-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-5′H-spiro-[chromeno[2,3-b]pyridine-5,4′-oxazol]-7-ol
(0.604 g, 1.592 mmol, 65.2% yield) as a tan solid. 1H NMR (400 MHz,
DMSO-d 6) δ = 9.35 (br s, 1 H), 8.31 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.73 (d, J =
2.4 Hz, 1 H), 7.08-7.00 (m, 1 H), 6.83-6.69 (m, 2 H), 6.50 (s, 2 H), 6.17
(t, J = 1.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.14 (s, 2 H), 3.83 (t, J = 5.4 Hz, 2 H), 2.40-2.32
(m, 2 H), 1.27 (s, 3 H), 1.27 (s, 3 H). MS m/z = 380.2 [M + H]+. Calcd
for C21H22N3O4: 380.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
