$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Cross-Coupling
Reactions To Afford Compounds 4, 7, and 8-40. To solution of aryl halid 6
or 7 (1.0 equiv) in 1,4-dioxan, the boronic acid (1.1 equiv) was added.
The mixture was thoroughly degassed with nitrogen for 15 min. Pd(PPh)3Cl2
(5-7 mol %) was added to the degassed solution under a nitrogen
atmosphere, followed by aqueous K2CO3 (1 M, 3.0 equiv). The reaction
mixture was stirred at 110°C for 16 h, poured into H2O, and extracted
with EtOAc (3×). The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried over MgSO4, and concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel Hexane/EtOAc. The product as solid.
6'-fluoro-5-(4-(methylsulfonyl)phenyl)-3,3'-bipyridin-2-amine (14) 65%
yield. m.p: 219-221°C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 8.47 (1H, d, J = 2.5
Hz), 8.37 (1H, d, J = 2.5 Hz), 8.12 (1H, td, J = 2.5, 8.5 Hz), 7.95 (4H,
m), 7.81 (1H, d, J = 2.5 Hz), 7.30 (1H, dd, J = 2.5, 8.5 Hz), 6.17 (2H,
br s), 3.23 (3H, s); 13C NMR (100 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ 164.0, 161.6, 157.7,
148.0, 147.1, 143.1, 139.0, 137.0, 132.4, 128.0 (2 × C), 126.5 (2 × C),
123.5, 116.6, 109.9, 44.1; Anal. RP-HPLC tR = 4.80 min (purity 97.5%);
LRMS (APCI): m/z = 344.0 [(M+H)+] (anal. calcd for C17H14FN3O2S+: m/z =
343.08).
