$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Palladium-Catalyzed
Cross-Coupling Reaction of Potassium Alkenyltrifluoroborates with
Brominated 2,1-Borazaronaphthalenes. To a Biotage 10 mL microwave vial
equipped with a magnetic stir bar were added
3-bromo-2,1-alkenyltrifluoroborate (1.1 mmol, 1.1 equiv), Cs2CO3 (3.0
mmol, 977 mg), Pd(dppf)Cl2 (6.0 mol %, 42 mg), and potassium
alkenyltrifluoroborate (1.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv). The vial was sealed with a
cap, lined with a Teflon septum, and evacuated and purged with argon gas
three times. Anhydrous degassed toluene (1.0 mL) and deionized H2O
(1.0mL) were added under argon gas. The reaction mixture was heated at
60°C for 18 h. After cooling to rt, the reaction mixture was extracted
with EtOAc (3 x 10 mL) and dried (MgSO4). After being concentrated in
vacuo, the product was isolated by flash column chromatography and eluted
with a gradient of EtOAc in hexanes (0 to 10% EtOAc).
tert-Butyl-4-[3-(2-methyl-2,1-borazaronaphthyl)]-3,6-dihydropyridine-1-(2H)-carboxylate
(3j). The title compound was obtained as a white solid in 65% yield
(210.6 mg). mp 83−87°C; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.75 (s, 1H), 7.69 (s,
1H), 7.57 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.36−7.33 (m, 1H), 7.17 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
1H), 7.14−7.11 (m, 1H), 5.71 (br, 1H), 4.07 (br, 2H), 3.64 (t, J = 5.5
Hz, 2H), 4.47 (br, 2H), 1.52 (s, 9H), 0.80 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125.8 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 155.3, 139.9, 139.6, 138.7, 129.5, 128.0, 125.1, 121.1, 120.7,
117.4, 79.7, 44.3, 40.1, 34.9, 29.4, 28.8; 11B NMR (128.38 MHz, CDCl3) δ
32.0; IR (neat) 3327, 2975, 1677, 1563, 1423, 1163 cm-1; HRMS (CI) m/z [M
+ H]+ calcd for C19H26BN2O2 325.2087, found 325.2080.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed vial used, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura Cross-Coupling of Brominated 2,1-Borazaronaphthalenes with
Potassium Alkenyltrifluoroborates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Molander, Gary A.; Wisniewski, Steven R.; Etemadi-Davan, Elham
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(22), 11199-11204

