$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-(6'-(2-Hydroxy-2-methylpropoxy)-4-((5-methylpyridin-3-yl)oxy)-[3,3'-bipyridin]-6-yl)-3-methylurea
(Step g, 27). A flask was charged with
1-(5-bromo-4-((5-methylpyridin-3-yl)oxy)pyridin-2-yl)-3-methylurea (10 g,
29.7 mmol),
2-methyl-1-((5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)pyridin-2-yl)oxy)propan-2-ol
(13.04 g, 44.5 mmol), tris (dibenzylideneacetone) dipalladium (0) (1.358
g, 1.483 mmol), tricyclohexylphosphine (0.832 g, 2.97 mmol) and
1,4-dioxane (100 mL). The mixture was flushed with Argon and added
potassium phosphate tribasic (20.49 g, 89 mmol) in water (15.00 mL). The
mixture was flushed with Ar and heated to 95°C for 1.5 h. The reaction
was cooled to room temperature and filtered through a Celite pad (the pad
was washed with 100 mL EtOAc). The solution was extracted with ethtyl
acetate (100 mL), washed with brine (50 mL) and water (50 mL), and
concentrated to afford the crude product. The crude solid was slurried in
EtOAc (150 mL) for 18 h, filtered, washed with EtOAc and dried 18 h. The
product as a cream colored solid (8.2g, 65%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
9.06 (s, 1H), 8.33 (s, 1H), 8.27 (m, 2H), 8.11 (s, 1H), 8.08 (s, 1H),
7.82 (dd, J = 8.6, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 7.22 (s, 1H), 6.88 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 1H),
6.11 (s, 1H), 4.25 (s, 2H), 2.87 (d, J = 4.5 Hz, 3H) 2.37 (s, 3H), 1.33
(s, 6H). Mass spectrum (apci) m/e = 423.9 (M+H).
