$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (a) 6-(2-Furyl)pyrazin-2-amine General Method A: Suzuki Couplings An oven
dried resealable Schlenk tube was charged with 6-chloropyrazin-2-amine
(0.73 g, 5.7 mmol), an aromatic boronic acid (7.4 mmol), dioxane (50 mL)
and a 2M aqueous solution of cesium carbonate 3 (8.5 mL, 17.1 mmol). The
Schlenk tube was subjected to three cycles of evacuation-backfilling with
argon, and 1,1'-bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene-palladium(II) dichloride
dichloromethane complex (PdCl2dppf) (0.29 g, 0.35 mmol) was added. After
three new cycles of evacuation-backfilling with argon, the Schlenk tube
was capped and stirred and heated to 90 °C. After 16h, the mixture was
cooled and partitioned between water and ethyl acetate and the aqueous
phase was extracted with further ethyl acetate. The combined organic
layer was washed with brine, dried (MgSO4) and evaporated. The desired
product was obtained after purification of the residue by flash
chromatography. (a) 6-(2-Furyl)pyrazin-2-amine Obtained as a yellow solid
(65%) from 6-chloropyrazin-2-ylamine and 2-furylboronic acid following
General Method A. δ 1H-NMR (CDCl3): 8.25 (s, 1H), 7.80 (s, 1H), 7.48 (d,
1H), 7.00 (d, 2H), 6.48 (m, 1H), 4.62 (bs, 2H).
