$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Independent Synthesis of 2-Methylbenzoxazole-5-Boronic Acid Pinacol Ester
In an argon-fed glove box, 7-bromo-2-methylbenzoxazole (30.3 mg, 0.143
mmol), B2pin2 (43.6 mg, 0.172 mmol), KOAc (42.4 mg, 0.433 mmol), and
PdCl2(dppf) (5.8 mg, 0.0071 mmol) were added to an oven-dried vial
equipped with a stir bar. To this vial was added DMF (0.5 mL). The vial
was sealed with a Teflon-lined cap and heated at 80 °C for 40 h. The
contents of the vial were poured into a separatory funnel, diluted with
ether (20 mL), and washed with water (3 x 20 mL). The organic layer was
dried over anhydrous sodium sulfate, filtered, and the solvent was
evaporated with a rotary evaporator. The residue was purified by flash
chromatography with 0- 20:100-80 EtOAc:hexanes as eluent, yielding of the
desired product. The 1H NMR and 13C NMR spectra were found to be
identical to those of product 5a (vide infra for tabulated chemical
shifts and spectra), confirming that iridium-catalyzed C-H borylation
occurred at the 7-position of 2-methylbenzoxazole. White solid, yield
24.1 mg (65%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, Miyaura Borylation reaction, glovebox
used, Teflon lined sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Iridium-Catalyzed C-H Borylation of Heteroarenes: Scope,
Regioselectivity, Application to Late-Stage Functionalization, and
Mechanism
